.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:105:| `create.sh` | Creates new Level 1 or phase folders from templates. It seeds the trigger phrases of the 15 template document kinds with the packet slug. After the documents are written, it replaces the planned `graph-metadata.json` stub with metadata derived from them through `backfill-graph-metadata.ts`, and a failed derivation warns and leaves the stub in place. With `--track`, it then runs `refresh-track-roots.mjs` for that track, so the new packet is listed in the track root's `children_ids` from the start. |
.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/README.md:107:| `validate.sh` | Runs the modular validation gate used before completion claims. `resolve_orchestrator()` checks the compiled runtime dist freshness (via `../lib/dist-freshness.cjs`) before trusting it and fails closed with exit `3` when stale: no silent auto-rebuild. A linked `upgrade-baseline.json` is not applied: the validator warns `UPGRADE_BASELINE_LINK` and the findings it would have downgraded stay errors. `--quiet` prints only the result line. On a `--strict` run, a Draft packet whose only errors are derived-metadata rules gets one `repair-derived.cjs --apply` and one revalidation, so the run can write files. `SPECKIT_DRAFT_AUTO_REPAIR=0` (or a set `CI`, or a `SPECKIT_RULES` subset) turns that off. |
